candidates.description:
Re-baseline the frozen tools in place, for contrast:
- edit CANONICAL to the advanced canonical;
- extend the new-file allowlists with foreign files, or switch them to a delta/merge-base check;
- re-pin the C8 approval record's canonical_head. This needs a new user approval record plus an APPROVAL_BLOB change in calibration_contracts.py, which changes CODE and therefore every acceptance hash.
A variant (T4) declares the tools non-applicable after integration.

candidates.decision_class:
D3, and also owner-only:
- §D5 (Frozen contract change);
- §N 'Track C Frozen phases' and 'canonical baseline';
- §K (rewrites Frozen tooling and a user approval record);
- §B (Track C owner lineage; tools/track_c_c8* is under the CDR-009/011 Codex exclusion);
- CDR-013 (no hard-coded SHA exception, no weakening).

The owner precedent (c84010c1 to a60c4c5f) only ever added newly approved Track C files and never re-pinned canonical, so it does not cover this.

D3:
- §D5 and §N (new Frozen acceptance meaning, recorded in the Track C scoped Decision Register, which is the authority per CDR-006);
- §B (Track C owner / Codex ownership; the CDR-009/011 exclusion covers tools/track_c_c8* for the PIW);
- CDR-013.

issues:
[HIGH, measured] The N2 pytest-config list is incomplete, and R1's pass rule can be met after Track C's Holdout and no-lookahead negative tests are silently deselected.
- pytest 9.1.1 (_pytest/config/findpaths) reads pytest.toml, .pytest.toml, pytest.ini, .pytest.ini, pyproject.toml, tox.ini and setup.cfg, and the first three outrank the others in the same directory.
- N2 lists only pytest.ini, tox.ini, setup.cfg, pyproject.toml and setup.py. It misses pytest.toml, .pytest.toml and .pytest.ini.
- R has no config file at all (only implementation/tests/conftest.py), so a foreign file becomes the inifile.
Measured at b9e01a9 on tests/test_evl_c8_contracts.py and tests/test_evl_c8_protocol.py:
- baseline: 76 passed;
- with a foreign implementation/tests/.pytest.toml, or implementation/.pytest.ini, setting addopts -k 'not holdout and not Holdout and not lookahead and not future': 69 passed, 7 deselected, 0 failed.
The deselected tests are exactly the Holdout and no-lookahead negatives:
- test_calibration_boundary_and_identity_fail_closed[holdout_role];
- test_no_lookahead_and_primary_stress_boundaries_before_content_access[future_feature, future_dataset, long_label, publication_equality];
- test_holdout_boundary_is_bound_to_current_registered_upstream_metadata;
- test_no_holdout_read_function_even_with_provider_argument.
R1 requires only failed=0, errors=0 and collected>0, so it PASSES. Regression coverage for I6 (PIT) and I8 (Holdout) is weakened without detection.

required_changes:
Add D3-5 for Track C's whole-package code identity on an integrated canonical, with options and a recommendation:
- (a) accept a new Track C code identity after each merge, with re-registration and new evidence;
- (b) the Track C owner scopes code identity to Track C's closure (a Frozen source change, §D5, owner plus user);
- (c) a merge freeze window.
State its effect on the recommended integration order explicitly.

Add negative controls:
- an empty foreign .py in another subpackage gives CODE_IDENTITY DIVERGED and the verdict is not PASS;
- a foreign pytest config that deselects tests makes R1 FAIL;
- pyc injection FAILs;
- an implementation/tools/__init__.py FAILs;
- an unattributed append to the Track C decision register FAILs;
- a broadened admitted-new prefix in R makes F2 FAIL.

Withdraw the claims 'order-independent' and 'no ordering decision is required'. Add a new D3 item: what happens when another capability appends to a shared overlay (CURRENT_HANDOFF, Master Status Index, Project Index, Contract Conflict Register, Artifact Evidence Register) or to HANDOFF_HISTORY before Track C lands. The options are:
- (a) a canonical ordering policy that Track C lands before any overlay-touching capability;
- (b) an interleaved-append attribution rule, which is a Frozen meaning or policy change;
- (c) fail-closed, case by case.
State that this does not bind any current PR (all ten non-Track C PR heads are add-only versus b8e39a2).
